The function will execute the summed string which becomes the input for the next function designed to parse an HTML document and extract information:
```javascript
function parseHtml(htmlString) {
    const parser = new DOMParser();
    const doc = parser.parseFromString(htmlString, 'text/html');
    return doc;
}
```
This function takes an HTML string, parses it, and returns the parsed document object.

To use these functions with SmartGPT, one would need to integrate them within a conversational interface or data processing workflow where the summed String from executeSum() serves as the parsed html Document in ParseHtml().
